    mv -nT <HOME>/.config/hypr <HOME>/.config/hypr.set-aside
    ricepilot rollback
    ricepilot rollback --commit

PROBLEM 3 of 3: <HOME>/.config/btop
  is a link ricepilot has no record of, where the generation before had it.
  rule: SAFETY.md, the ownership predicate (fact 3: the ledger must record it)

  it points at
    <HOME>/rice/new/btop

  generation 0001, the one `rescue.sh` restores, had exactly this link;
  the current generation had none, and the ledger has no row for it.
  most likely the script put it back. every switch and rollback refuses
  it until it is set aside and the rollback links it again.

  run:
    # set it aside (nothing is lost); the rollback links it again
    mv -nT <HOME>/.config/btop <HOME>/.config/btop.set-aside
    ricepilot rollback
    ricepilot rollback --commit

